From: locateanything-perf
Subject: hybrid generation_mode never falls back to AR on text, so every
         transcription is garbled

nvidia/LocateAnything-3B, generate_utils.py + modeling_locateanything.py.
Apply inside the downloaded model directory:

    patch -p0 -d $LA_MODEL < patches/04-hybrid-ar-fallback-on-text.patch
    rm -rf "$HF_HOME/modules/transformers_modules"     # REQUIRED, see below

WHAT IS WRONG

The model card documents three decode modes:

    'fast'   : MTP only, never fall back to AR
    'slow'   : AR only, pure auto-regressive decoding
    'hybrid' : MTP first, fall back to AR on error, switch back on box_end

and recommends hybrid. hybrid never falls back. On a scanned book page it
produces output byte-identical to fast -- 1641 characters either way, 5.14s vs
5.10s -- and both read

    "during the centuries that the taken theirionalional located flight"

where the same page under 'slow' reads

    "during the centuries that have taken their processional flight"

It is not a trigger that fails to fire. It is a check that was never written.
handle_pattern() returns "error_box" from exactly one of its five branches --
the one handling <box> -- and error_box is the only value the generate loop
tests to leave MTP. The branch that handles prose returns

    {"type": "ref_object", "tokens": x0, "need_switch_to_ar": False}

i.e. six speculatively-decoded tokens accepted whole, with no verification of
any kind. That is sound for coordinates: <box><x0><y0><x1><y1></box> nearly
determines its own continuation, so a wrong guess produces a malformed pattern
that IS detectable and does become error_box. Prose has no such structure, so a
wrong guess is simply emitted. The stutter is the six-token block boundary.

A second defect blocks the obvious one-line fix. hybrid's AR phase only ever ran
as a rescue from a malformed box, so it assumes it is inside one:

    if   token_val == box_end_token_id:                 out_type = 'box_end_ar'
    elif coord_start <= token_val <= coord_end:         out_type = 'coord_ar'
    else:                                               out_type = 'im_end'

Route text there and the first letter of a <ref> is read as end-of-sequence and
the response stops dead. Both halves have to change together.

WHY REGION COUNTS NEVER CAUGHT IT

All four paths return 28 regions on this page, within 25 characters of each
other. The boxes are correct in every mode -- only the transcribed text differs.
Any benchmark that counts boxes scores the garbled run and the clean run
identically.

WHAT THIS COSTS

Correct text is slower, because text now decodes one token per forward instead
of six. Measured on the same page, RTX 3090, bf16:

    hybrid before   5.14s   garbled
    hybrid after   19.36s   clean, 28 regions, 1621 chars
    slow           22.67s   clean, 28 regions, 1619 chars

The patched hybrid beats pure AR because coordinates still go through MTP:
ref_end_ar hands control back at </ref>, so the box that follows is decoded six
tokens at a time as before.

Detection is unaffected in output and costs 5.3%: 16 photographs at 10,000
patches, 16.72s -> 17.60s, identical box counts on all 16. The cost there is
routing four tokens of <ref>cats</ref> through AR.

THE trust_remote_code TRAP

transformers executes a COPY of the model's python under
$HF_HOME/modules/transformers_modules, not the files in the model directory.
Patching the model directory without clearing that cache appears to work and
changes nothing. Clear it, or the patch never runs.

--- generate_utils.py	2026-08-23 22:04:55.093390626 -0400
+++ generate_utils.py	2026-08-23 22:05:19.470877553 -0400
@@ -496,6 +496,26 @@
         if len(x0) >= 2 and x0[-1] == x0[-2] == ref_end_token_id:
             x0 = x0[:-1]
 
+        if generation_mode == 'hybrid':
+            # This branch is prose -- the contents of a <ref>. MTP predicted six
+            # of them in one forward, and nothing above verified any of it. That
+            # is sound for the box branch, where <box><x0><y0><x1><y1></box>
+            # nearly determines its own continuation and a wrong guess shows up
+            # as a malformed pattern that becomes error_box. Text has no such
+            # structure, so a wrong guess is simply emitted, which is why
+            # hybrid transcription reads "traveled traveled to the four corners
+            # of earth earth" while pure AR reads it correctly.
+            #
+            # Keep only the first token -- the one position the forward actually
+            # conditioned on real context -- and hand the rest to AR, exactly as
+            # error_box already does for a malformed box.
+            return {
+                "type": "text_ar",
+                "tokens": x0[:1],
+                "need_switch_to_ar": True,
+                "is_terminal": False,
+            }
+
         return {
             "type": "ref_object",
             "tokens": x0,
